# =============================================================================
# .gitignore - Bug Squash Arena
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rule of thumb: commit SOURCE and TEMPLATES, never generated output or SECRETS.
# Anything that `npm ci`, `vite build` or `docker compose` can recreate stays out
# of Git; anything that contains a real password or token MUST stay out of Git.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Dependencies (recreated by `npm ci` from package-lock.json) -------------
node_modules/

# ---- Build output (recreated by `npm run build` / the Docker "build" stage) --
dist/
build/
coverage/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Secrets / environment files ---------------------------------------------
# Real env files hold passwords and JWT secrets. They are created by copying a
# template on each machine and are NEVER committed:
#   cp .env.example .env               (local development)
#   cp .env.prod.example .env.prod     (production server)
#   .env.ci is a throwaway file written by the ci-test workflow.
.env
.env.*
# ...but the templates themselves are documentation and MUST be committed.
# The "!" prefix re-includes a file that an earlier pattern excluded.
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example

# ---- Logs ---------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ---- Runtime / misc -----------------------------------------------------------
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock
.eslintcache
.npm/
tmp/
*.tmp

# ---- OS junk ------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---- Editors / IDEs ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.sublime-workspace
.history/
